    {
      "id": "srs8k6s",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Disease"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Diseases are broadly classified into communicable (infectious) and non-communicable (non-infectious) conditions.",
        "Communicable diseases spread through pathogens like bacteria, viruses, fungi, and protozoa via vectors or direct contact.",
        "Deficiency diseases occur due to an insufficient intake of essential nutrients, vitamins, or minerals.",
        "The immune system comprises innate (present from birth) and acquired (developed through exposure/vaccination) immunity.",
        "Vaccination induces active immunity by introducing harmless antigens to stimulate antibody production."
      ],
      "id": "3lupi17"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bi56fdd",
      "content": "• A disease is a condition that impairs normal body function."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "c43pf88",
      "content": "• It may cause pain, weakness, discomfort or dysfunction of organs."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "kn2b2oh",
      "content": "• Diseases may be infectious or non‑infectious."
    },
    {
      "id": "009aj4d",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Types of Diseases"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6jkmagf",
      "content": "• Communicable diseases – Spread from one person to another."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mthvpqn",
      "content": "• Non‑communicable diseases – Do not spread between individuals."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ml2mbqr",
      "content": "• Deficiency diseases – Caused by lack of nutrients."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jxu8zz3",
      "content": "• Hereditary diseases – Passed through genes."
    },
    {
