    {
      "id": "6pdz0xa",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Vaccination"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "btw38te",
      "content": "• Vaccines stimulate the immune system to produce antibodies."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1ym8x0a",
      "content": "• They protect against diseases such as polio, measles and hepatitis."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "j3ayfbs",
      "content": "• Vaccination is one of the most effective methods of disease prevention."
    },
    {
      "id": "ndgb0d0",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. Prevention of Diseases"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ehly2x3",
      "content": "• Maintain personal hygiene."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hicfq5l",
      "content": "• Eat a balanced diet."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "r4ajuha",
      "content": "• Drink clean water."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Frequently tested: Distinguish between active immunity (long-lasting, produced by body) and passive immunity (short-term, ready-made antibodies).",
        "Memory trick for competitive exams: Link major deficiency diseases to specific vitamins/minerals (e.g., Vitamin D – Rickets, Iodine – Goitre).",
        "Pay attention to disease vectors: Female Anopheles causes Malaria; Aedes aegypti transmits Dengue and Chikungunya."
      ],
      "id": "tiawdmx"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "miscz21",
      "content": "• Regular vaccination."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2a8pi4f",
      "content": "• Control insects and mosquitoes."
    },
    {
      "id": "tbe3rrt",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ogeezpo",
      "content": "• Vaccines help build immunity."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dsdnlgz",
      "content": "• Vitamin deficiencies cause several diseases."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "aaxhwkm",
      "content": "• Pathogens include bacteria, viruses, fungi and parasites."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9446p8f",
      "content": "• The immune system defends the body against infections."
    }
  ],
